Core Objective & Scope
We are building a multi-tenant QR loyalty platform for white-label clients. The product is a SaaS-style system where end users scan a shared QR, verify their phone by OTP, earn points, and redeem rewards; tenants get independent branding and rules. The first product category is plywood, but the core architecture must support future white-label expansion.

Target end state:

One deployment, one Postgres DB, with tenant-scoped data access.
Shared QR-based customer flow with pending points against device tokens.
OTP verification with mock mode for local dev and tests.
Append-only points ledger with FIFO redemption and expiry logic.
Rewards catalog starting with vouchers but schema-ready for product rewards.
Separate admin auth and tenant-scoped admin UI.
Browser-first SaaS admin flow; PWA is optional later, not required for v1.
Mobile-first user flow, no native app in scope for now.
