Decisions Made & Constraints
Technical decisions finalized:

Admin UI will be role-specific but share one backend and one design system.
Settings use a hybrid model:
key/value table with explicit required keys for v1
flexible enough for future config additions
Rewards schema is product-ready, but implementation starts with vouchers only.
Custom domains are deferred; slug routing is the first and correct tenant identity path.
Browser-first admin SaaS experience, with optional PWA installability later.
Use separate login/session flows for user and admin.
Do not infer user vs admin screen from phone number; determine by role/session.
User data must remain isolated by tenant; same phone in different tenants is distinct.
Constraints and rules:

Every table must contain tenant_id.
No query may run without a tenant context.
Never mutate ledger rows; append-only only.
Balance is derived, never stored as source of truth.
Redemptions must be atomic with idempotency key and DB row locking.
Use Redis as a control/cache layer, not the source of truth.
Local mock OTP only when MSG91_AUTH_KEY is empty or absent.
Do not add speculative abstractions beyond current phase.
Do not overbuild; keep Phase 1 minimal and stable.
No custom domains, payment gateways, native apps, or product delivery tools in v1.
